## 4. BACKEND SPEC (Google Apps Script)

### 4.1 API contract
- Deploy as Web App: Execute as **Me**, Access **Anyone**. Because Apps Script cannot read custom headers or handle CORS preflight, the client sends **`POST` with `Content-Type: text/plain;charset=utf-8`** and a JSON body: `{ "action": "...", "token": "...", "payload": {...}, "reqId": "..." }`.
- Response always: `{ ok: boolean, data?: any, error?: { code, message }, reqId }`. Use stable error codes (`AUTH_REQUIRED`, `SESSION_EXPIRED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `VALIDATION`, `NOT_FOUND`, `LOCKED`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `CONFLICT`, `SERVER`).
- A single dispatcher maps `action` to a handler; each handler declares its required permission key(s), scope resolver, field-level rules and whether it writes. Unknown actions return `NOT_FOUND`.
- `doGet` returns only a minimal health JSON (no data).
- A **public** action `public.config` returns ONLY safe branding and login-page data (company name, logo URL, theme tokens, background config, login notice text, language default). Never any employee or internal data.

### 4.2 Authentication and sessions
- Passwords: per-user random salt + a server-side pepper in Script Properties + **iterated SHA-256 (HMAC)** using `Utilities`. Tune iterations so login stays well within Apps Script time limits; document the value. Never store or log plain passwords.
- Session token: cryptographically random (UUID/`Utilities.getUuid()` combined with random bytes). Store **only the hash** of the token in `Sessions` with employee ID, created, last seen, expiry (idle timeout and absolute timeout, configurable), device/user-agent hash. Support logout and "logout all devices".
- Brute-force protection: per Employee ID and global rate limiting using CacheService/Sheet counters; temporary lock after configurable failed attempts; audit every failure. Do not reveal whether the Employee ID exists.
- First login and any admin password reset force a password change. Password policy configurable (min length, complexity). Reset only by users with `user.resetpassword`.
- All write operations use `LockService` with timeout handling and return `LOCKED` with a retry hint on failure.

### 4.3 Database (Google Sheets, accessed only through `Database.gs`)
Two spreadsheets, IDs stored in Script Properties:
- **HRMS_CORE_DB** and yearly **HRMS_ATTENDANCE_<YEAR>** (auto-created by trigger on 1 January and on demand).

Core tabs (create with headers, data validation where useful, frozen header row, protected from manual editing):
- Core: `Users, Employees, Departments, Designations, Branches`
- Access: `Roles, Permissions_Catalog, Role_Permissions, User_Role_Map, User_Permission_Overrides, Delegations, Feature_Flags, Sessions`
