## 7. ATTENDANCE: GEO-FENCING (OFFICE ONLY) AND OPTIONAL SELFIE

- Each employee has an **Attendance Policy** (Office Geo-fenced, Site/Field, Exempt/Flexible, or custom). Geo-fencing applies **only** when the policy requires it. Site/field policies never request location.
- Geo-fence parameters are data: `Geofence_Locations` (lat, lng, radius in meters; multiple points per branch), minimum GPS accuracy, geo-fence on check-out (optional), outside behavior (Block or Flag + manager approval), GPS-denied behavior, check-in window.
- Browser sends `lat, lng, accuracy, timestamp`. **Server** computes Haversine distance and decides. Time is always **server time**. Store inside/outside, distance, accuracy; keep raw coordinates only for the retention period set in Settings, then purge by trigger.
- Anomaly flags: repeated identical coordinates, impossible travel, very low accuracy. Flags go to the manager/HR inbox.
- **Selfie is an optional feature** controlled by Feature Switches at company, policy and employee levels (employee overrides policy overrides company). When OFF, no camera UI appears. When ON, capture in-app (`getUserMedia`, fallback to file input with `capture`), compress to a small JPEG client-side, upload, store in private Drive folder by month, link by file ID. Viewing requires `selfie.view`. Auto-delete after the configured retention. **No face recognition.**
- Before first use of location or selfie, show a consent screen; record version and time in `Consent_Log`. No consent, no capture.
- Shifts, grace, late rules, half-day rules, minimum hours, weekly off, holidays, comp-off, overtime (approved only), missed check-out handling, regularization with monthly limit, on-duty/tour requests, month lock (corrections after lock only via approval). All configurable.
- Supervisors/authorised users can **mark attendance on behalf** (permission and scope controlled, flagged and audited).
- Be honest in the UI and docs: a browser cannot detect mock-GPS apps. Document this limitation and the mitigations (accuracy limit, anomaly flags, optional selfie, spot checks).

